This project is a clean-room, vendor-neutral open-source work. It is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or derived from the internal systems of any
employer or company. Any resemblance to a specific organization's internal
architecture is coincidental; all control names in the experiment catalog are
generic, industry-standard concepts (service mesh, API gateway, KMS, etc.).

The design draws on publicly described ideas from the Security Chaos Engineering
community, including:
  - "Security Chaos Engineering" by Kelly Shortridge & Aaron Rinehart (O'Reilly).
  - The UUID-correlation detonate-then-assert pattern popularized by Datadog's
    open-source Threatest and Stratus Red Team projects.
  - The reusable-definition / bound-intent CRD separation popularized by the
    CNCF LitmusChaos and Chaos Mesh projects.
These are credited as inspiration; no third-party code is vendored here unless
listed in go.mod with its own upstream license.
